# AirTulip — heading capitalization (Title Case)

When you **write or edit heading text** in this theme, capitalize the **first letter of every word**. This applies to headings only—not body copy, richtext paragraphs, button labels, or schema info strings unless they are clearly a heading field.

## Scope — what counts as a heading

- Section/block settings named like `heading`, `title`, `top_heading`, `bottom_heading`, `overlay_heading`, `subheading` when used as a visible headline (h1–h6 or theme `.heading` classes)
- JSON template values in `templates/*.json` and section presets that populate headline fields
- Liquid-visible headlines in `sections/`, `blocks/`, and `snippets/`
- Marketing page copy you add for heroes, split-text headlines, multicolumn titles, CTAs with headline styling

**Do not** apply this rule to long-form body text, FAQ answers, product descriptions, or `description` / `text` richtext fields.

## Rule

- **Title Case every word** in headings the agent creates or rewrites.
- Keep existing merchant-edited headings unchanged unless the task is to rewrite that heading.

## Exceptions (keep canonical form)

| Keep as-is | Examples |
|------------|----------|
| Brand / product names | AirTulip, AirTulip Sleep |
| Acronyms & grades | H14, HEPA, dB(A), PM2.5 |
| Already-styled trademarks | TrueMed, Shark Tank |
| Numbers and symbols | 1,000×, 26, U.S. |

When a proper noun is mid-heading, still capitalize its first letter if the brand style allows (e.g. **Shop AirTulip Sleep**).

## Examples

| Avoid | Use |
|-------|-----|
| Stop breathing the room. Start breathing clean. | Stop Breathing The Room. Start Breathing Clean. |
| Built to a standard, not a price point. | Built To A Standard, Not A Price Point. |
| Scientifically proven results | Scientifically Proven Results |
| Over 1,000× cleaner | Over 1,000× Cleaner |

Body copy under the heading stays in normal sentence case:

- Heading: **Particles Per Breath Drop To Cleanroom-Level Performance While You Sleep.**
- Body: *Particles per breath drop to cleanroom-level performance while you sleep.*

